  "id": "COMPOUND:21451 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may interact with M19-MEL, through a series of target-mediated pathways. The drug is linked to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a known target of multiple compounds, including WS-5995 B and (Salicylato-O1,O2)silver. These compounds, in turn, target M19-MEL, indicating a possible pathway involving proteasome regulation. The presence of multiple overlapping targets suggests that Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may modulate proteasome activity, potentially influencing the degradation of proteins that regulate M19-MEL. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the drug and M19-MEL, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The consistent targeting of the 26S proteasome subunit across different compounds implies a broader role in the drug's mechanism, though further investigation is needed to confirm the specific molecular interactions.",
